xt","field","captureDate","label","Screenshot captured","value","2026-10-18","image","gameplay","Browser capture during a run after starting and jumping, with a live distance counter.","src","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/running-man-claude-pixellab.webp","alt","Running Man character crossing a scrolling road beneath a pixel-art mountain landscape.","https://games.jdilig.me/games/running-man/","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","GameMap browser capture","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)","items",[82],"Claude Code","links","Related resources",[88,89],"resourceIds","section",{"_59":82,"_27":92},{"_59":90,"_27":91},"PixelLab AI Agent Toolkit","/resources/pixellab/","/resources/claude-code/","Creator evidence",[96],"evidence",{"_59":97,"_27":98,"_99":100},"Read the tool and asset disclosure","https://github.com/balbonits/ai-browser-game-demos#tools-used","note","The creator identifies Claude Code, PixelLab, synthesized audio, and human direction.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[105],{"_59":106,"_27":107,"_99":108},"Open the game collection source","https://github.com/balbonits/ai-browser-game-demos","Self-contained games with code, PixelLab assets, sound synthesis, and per-game notes.","Access type","playable","demo","Play or run",[114],{"_59":115,"_27":70,"_99":116},"Play Running Man","Space, Up, W, or tap starts and jumps. P or Esc pauses; R retries after death.","Game platform","Browser","Guide format","build log","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[124],{"_59":125,"_27":126,"_99":-7},"Read the game’s development notes","https://github.com/balbonits/ai-browser-game-demos/blob/main/docs/games/running-man.md","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[131,132,133],"Play a run and test jumping, death, retry, and pause.","Read the per-game notes and asset inventory.","Compare animation frames and obstacle hitboxes with the renderer and collision code.","AI workflow / foundation context","John Dilig attributes the game code to Claude Code and the pixel art to PixelLab via MCP, under human direction. Per-game notes document the assets and subsequent changes.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-generated (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","2D","track","metadata","Engine","Canvas 2D · JavaScript","engine","lead","2d","ai-generated",[131,132,133],{"_59":125,"_27":126,"_19":162},{"_59":115,"_27":70,"_19":110,"_99":116},{"_59":106,"_27":107,"_99":108,"_160":161},{"_59":97,"_27":98,"_99":100},[158,159],"claude-code","pixellab","scope","complete-project","build-log","example:katana-kitsune-godot","katana-kitsune-godot","Katana Kitsune: Prototype","Choose a kitsune fighter and face yokai in an isometric action roguelike with katana combat, stamina, pickups and successive dungeon floors. The silent prototype supports local multiplayer, with additional party systems documented in the current source.","/examples/katana-kitsune-godot/",{"_21":164,"_23":165,"_25":166,"_148":252,"_144":150,"_140":253,"_136":242,"_247":254,"_9":255,"_121":256,"_111":257,"_34":258,"_95":259,"_86":260},[170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190],{"_55":23,"_61":165,"_57":23,"_87":-7},{"_55":149,"_61":166,"_57":25,"_87":-7},{"_55":56,"_59":146,"_61":252,"_57":148,"_87":137},{"_55":77,"_59":244,"_128":245,"_80":246,"_57":247,"_87":-7},{"_55":56,"_59":142,"_61":143,"_57":144,"_87":145},{"_55":56,"_59":138,"_61":243,"_57":140,"_87":141},{"_55":56,"_59":134,"_61":242,"_57":136,"_87":137},{"_55":77,"_59":127,"_128":129,"_80":237,"_57":9,"_87":-7},{"_55":83,"_59":122,"_80":233,"_57":121,"_87":-7},{"_55":56,"_59":119,"_61":120,"_57":121,"_87":-7},{"_55":56,"_59":117,"_61":232,"_57":111,"_87":-7},{"_55":83,"_59":112,"_80":228,"_57":111,"_87":-7},{"_55":56,"_59":109,"_61":110,"_57":111,"_87":-7},{"_55":83,"_59":103,"_80":223,"_57":34,"_87":-7},{"_55":56,"_59":101,"_61":102,"_57":34,"_87":-7},{"_55":83,"_59":93,"_80":218,"_57":95,"_87":-7},{"_55":83,"_59":84,"_80":206,"_57":86,"_87":-7},{"_55":77,"_57":78,"_59":79,"_80":204},{"_55":63,"_57":64,"_59":199,"_66":200,"_68":201,"_34":202,"_71":72,"_73":74,"_75":203},{"_55":56,"_57":196,"_59":197,"_61":198},{"_55":83,"_57":191,"_59":192,"_80":193},"originalImage","Original creator image",[194],{"_59":192,"_27":195},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune/bc9321eeaac727bbb5372a315ec58f68c96240ac/marketing/itch/05_attack.png","mediaReviewed","Screenshot source reviewed","2026-10-20","Creator-published combat screenshot from the silent Godot prototype.","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/katana-kitsune-godot.webp","The creator’s Katana Kitsune combat screenshot with an isometric courtyard, the party, enemies, health bars and minimap.","https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune/blob/bc9321eeaac727bbb5372a315ec58f68c96240ac/marketing/itch/05_attack.png","Creator-published screenshot",[82,205],"GitHub Copilot",[207,208,209,210,211],{"_59":82,"_27":92},{"_59":216,"_27":217},{"_59":90,"_27":91},{"_59":214,"_27":215},{"_59":212,"_27":213},"Blender","/resources/blender/","Meshy API","/resources/meshy/","Godot Engine · Official Documentation","/resources/godot-engine/",[219],{"_59":220,"_27":221,"_99":222},"Read the creator’s AI production disclosure","https://9-k9.itch.io/katanakitsune","The author explicitly names Claude Code and GitHub Copilot alongside image, sprite and 3D asset tools, and links the primary complete source repository. The README verifies the Godot version and explains which finished assets are included.",[224],{"_59":225,"_27":226,"_99":227},"Open the complete Godot game project","https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune","Godot 4.7 project with scenes, GDScript, Dialogic addon and finished sprite assets. The inspected tree contains about 383 MB of files; no top-level game license was found. The upstream Meshy/Blender/PixelOver authoring pipeline is separate, while its finished runtime sprites are committed. The current source contains newer party/asset changes than the reviewed hosted prototype.",[229],{"_59":230,"_27":221,"_99":231},"Play Katana Kitsune on itch.io","Silent HTML5 prototype with keyboard and gamepad support. Space confirms player/device choices; allow a clear press and release between setup steps. The browser build loaded and reached player/device selection in review; combat and a complete dungeon run were not exercised. The download is large: about 184 MB of game data plus 40 MB of WebAssembly.","itch.io",[234],{"_59":235,"_27":236,"_99":-7},"Read the game and asset-pipeline documentation","https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune#readme",[238,239,240,241],"Open the itch prototype and choose one human player, then claim a keyboard and select a costume.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and the repository’s character, combat and sprite-pipeline notes.","Open project.godot in Godot 4.7 using GL Compatibility; the finished sprites and game scenes are included.","Change one combat or spawn setting, then check the title-to-character-to-dungeon flow, damage and restart.","The creator identifies Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, GPT Image 2, PixelLab and Meshy among the production tools. The repository documents Meshy rigs and animation, Blender retargeting and PixelOver sprite exports. The exact coding models and division of code between assistants are not specified; generated NPC teammates are not the evidence for AI-assisted development.","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","Asset creation tools",false,[248,249,250,212,251],"assetTools","GPT Image 2","PixelLab","Meshy","PixelOver","Godot 4.7 · GDScript · 2D / GL Compatibility","ai-assisted",[248,249,250,212,251],[238,239,240,241],{"_59":235,"_27":236,"_19":162},{"_59":230,"_27":221,"_19":110,"_99":231},{"_59":225,"_27":226,"_160":161,"_99":227},{"_59":220,"_27":221,"_99":222},[158,261,159,262,263],"godot-engine","meshy","blender","resource:pixellab","resource","Generates pixel characters, animation, and seamless tilesets through API and M